Thought: Evaluate the dataset‑level meta‑model weights.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w5","rationale":"dataset‑level meta‑model"}  
Thought: Evaluate the inverse‑error weights on pool3.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w6","rationale":"inverse‑error on pool3"}

Thought: test inverse‑error weighting on pool3 to see if it beats the current leader (weighted w1).  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w6","rationale":"inverse‑error weighting on pool3"}  

Thought: add shrinkage to reduce variance; create a new handle on pool3 with shrinkage 0.1.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool3","shrinkage":0.1,"metric":"rmse"}  

Thought: evaluate the new weighted strategy with shrinkage.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w8","rationale":"inverse‑error with shrinkage 0.1 on pool3"}

Thought: I’ll start by evaluating the unscored weight handle w2 to see if a different weighting scheme can beat the current best weighted w1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w2"}

Thought: evaluate the shrinkage‑weighted pool2 (w7) to see if the regularisation improves over w2.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w7","rationale":"test shrinkage on stable pool"}

Thought: The weighted strategy using handle w1 on the full pool gives the lowest validation score (0.6557) and is statistically indistinguishable from the runner‑up, so we select it as the final combination.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1","rationale":"final choice"}

